      "start": 0.62,
      "end": 1.86,
      "text": "Hi, how have you been?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.56,
      "end": 15.12,
      "text": "Those are probably fungus gnats. They breed in damp compost, and the larvae live in the top layer of soil."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 18.68,
      "end": 22.74,
      "text": "Mostly they're just annoying, though lots of larvae can nibble seedling roots."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 25.67,
      "end": 32.73,
      "text": "Let the top few centimetres dry out between waterings, that breaks their cycle. Yellow sticky traps catch the adults."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 39.25,
      "end": 46.61,
      "text": "That's a common one. Try watering from below, standing the pots in a tray for twenty minutes. The surface stays dry and the gnats give up."
    }
  ]
